  "Question": "What is \\((-1)^1 + (-1)^2 + \\cdots + (-1)^{2006}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2006\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(2006\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Odd powers of \\(-1\\) equal \\(-1\\), and even powers equal \\(1\\). Pair each odd-exponent term with the following even-exponent term:\n\\[\n\\bigl((-1)^1+(-1)^2\\bigr)+\\cdots+\n\\bigl((-1)^{2005}+(-1)^{2006}\\bigr).\n\\]\nThere are \\(2006/2=1003\\) pairs, each with sum \\(-1+1=0\\), and no term is left over. Therefore the sum is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice C.",
